Today at the office, I drink coffee with Rohan.
I inform him of Saturday's plan.
"Priya invited me to her house for dinner," I say.
"Oh, that is very good," Rohan says.
"I will go to her house by metro," I say.
I think that the metro journey will be easy.
"Yes, the metro is very convenient," Rohan says.
Then I ask him.
"Rohan, what will I bring there?"
"I do not know Indian traditions," I say.
Rohan smiles and drinks coffee.
"You can bring a small box of Indian sweets," he says.
"Everyone likes sweets."
I think that this is a good idea.
"I will buy Kaju Katli sweets," I say.
"That is my favourite sweet!"
"Priya will definitely be happy," Rohan says.
He finishes his coffee.
"Come, now let's work again," he says.
